EDA findings: 26 species have zero training signal anywhere — how are you handling them?
Spent time doing a deep EDA and found a few things I hadn't seen discussed yet:

It's not just 28 missing species — 26 have NO data at all 28 species in the submission have no train_audio clips. But when you check train_soundscapes_labels.csv, only 2 appear there. The other 26 — mostly the 25 "Insect sonotype" classes plus Chiasmocleis mehelyi — have absolutely zero training signal anywhere in the provided data.
With Macro ROC-AUC every species counts equally. Ignoring them means a guaranteed 0 on 26/234 classes.

Only 0.6% of soundscapes are labeled 10,658 soundscape files exist but only 66 are labeled. That's 10,592 files of Pantanal audio with no labels — the exact domain the test set comes from.

Geographic shift is real Training recordings are global (lat: -54 to +69). Test is Pantanal-specific. Most training data is Northern Hemisphere.

Full breakdown with charts here: https://www.kaggle.com/code/kodatirevanth/birdclef-2026-eda-beginner-s-deep-dive

Has anyone found a strategy for the 26 completely unlabeled insect sonotypes? Curious what approaches people are trying.


